@model ActionEditorModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Action editor"; }
<h1>Action editor</h1>
<p>Steps execute in order. Every step requires a fixed deployment ID, or an explicit Agent ID for host-exec. Editing changes execution ownership to you. Saved runs retain an immutable plan.</p>
<form method="post" action="/automation/actions/edit">@Html.AntiForgeryToken()
<div asp-validation-summary="All"></div><input asp-for="Id" type="hidden" /><input asp-for="Revision" type="hidden" />
<label asp-for="Name"></label><input asp-for="Name" />
<label><input asp-for="Enabled" /> Enabled</label>
<label asp-for="Concurrency"></label><select asp-for="Concurrency"><option value="queue">Queue conflicting action runs</option><option value="reject">Reject overlapping runs</option></select>
<label asp-for="PlanJson">Action plan JSON</label><textarea asp-for="PlanJson" rows="25" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
<button type="submit">Save action</button></form>
<h2>Plan format and safety</h2>
<p>Supported kinds: git-refresh, validate, build, pull, deploy, start, stop, restart, remove, status, logs, container-exec, host-exec. Git refresh resolves and checks out configured sources into an isolated operation snapshot, then validates Compose; it requires both sources.manage and deployment.validate. It does not edit managed files or create a shared mutable checkout. Build/deploy also resolve their own immutable source snapshots. Each step supports timeoutSeconds (1–3600) and failure (stop/continue). Cancel stops remaining steps and requests cancellation of the active operation; side effects are not rolled back.</p>
<pre>{"steps":[{"kind":"container-exec","deploymentId":"DEPLOYMENT_ID","timeoutSeconds":60,"failure":"stop","execution":{"executable":"/usr/bin/printf","arguments":["%s","${message}"],"service":"app","container":null,"user":"1000","workingDirectory":"/app","environment":{"MODE":"safe"}}}],"parameters":[{"name":"message","type":"string","required":true,"default":null}]}</pre>
<p>Parameters support string, integer and boolean types. Optional integer/boolean parameters require a typed default. A parameter can replace only one entire argument, never an executable, target, environment value, or part of an argument. No shell is inserted. Interpreter steps may contain deliberately authored fixed scripts, but cannot accept external parameter substitutions.</p>
<p><strong>Host prerequisites:</strong> host-exec needs a separate host.execute grant and an approved Agent with explicitly enabled host execution and an isolated host execution adapter. An Agent-container command is never host execution. The operation fails if this capability is not available; Stanza never enables host privileges automatically.</p>
<p>Container steps select exactly one service or container. Missing or stopped targets fail; they are never automatically started by exec.</p>
